              "index": 1,
              "count": 10,
              "title": "Knowledge Meets the Open World",
              "narration": "The earliest kaaroViewer is built on an implicit assumption: knowledge worth visualizing exists in the open world. OpenTapioca matches text to Wikidata QIDs; SPARQL fetches structured facts — descriptions, images, linked identifiers. For public subjects, this works precisely because Wikidata already knows them. The system renders what it can look up.",
              "tension": "low",
              "accent": "#f05500",
