            "duration": 29.8,
            "params": {
              "index": 5,
              "count": 10,
              "title": "Ontology Drift — The Liability of LLM Freedom",
              "narration": "Left unconstrained, the LLM invents types and relationships the renderer does not understand. Two documents on the same topic, encoded weeks apart, produce incompatible schemas. Early encodings produce edge densities as low as 1.32; others reach 2.41. The gap is not quality variance — it is ontological incoherence. Drift becomes the dominant library failure mode.",
              "tension": "high",
              "accent": "#f05500",
              "docTitle": "kaaroViewer: A Self-Governing Spatial Intelligence Platform",
              "graph": {
