              "title": "The Ontology Problem Is Named, Not Solved",
              "narration": "9 library entries. 168 tests passing. 1 Dream Loop run complete. The ontology problem — maintaining a stable, evolvable, personalized vocabulary for private knowledge visualization — is now explicit and partially constrained. The vocabulary extension mechanism exists; the gaps that require it lie ahead. The eval loop surfaces the gap between ontological correctness (validator pass) and ontological quality (faithful encoding). The system is self-aware of its own limits.",
